# Normalise line endings across every machine.
#
# Without this, Windows defaults to autocrlf=true, which converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout. The result is noisy whole-file diffs when contributors switch
# between operating systems, and "the file changed but nothing changed" commits.
#
# Rule: everything is LF in the working tree, except Windows scripts, which
# genuinely require CRLF to execute.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Treat these as binary — never let git try to normalise them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Lockfiles are machine-generated; never resolve merge conflicts in them by hand.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff
